  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The query is sulfisoxazole (3,4-dimethyl-5-isoxazolyl sulfanilamide); the closest supplied analog is sulfamethoxazole, for which L3 oral-exposure records show substantial systemic exposure after oral dosing (AUC 39.07 µg·h/mL at 60 mg/kg p.o., C111; AUC 25.9 µg·h/mL at 30 mg/kg p.o., C118; Cmax 60.9 mg/L, C104).",
      "card_ids": ["C111","C118","C104"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 records for the sulfanilamide/isoxazole class consistently show high fraction absorbed: sulfamethoxazole absorption increased in disease (C135), sulfamethizole 85% Fa (C175) with Caco-2 permeability (C177), sulfapyridine almost complete absorption (C131, C156, C166), sulfamethazine practically complete absorption (C154, C172) and 99.2% relative absorption as an oral solution (C141), and sulfadimethoxine well absorbed (C153).",
      "card_ids": ["C135","C175","C177","C131","C156","C166","C154","C172","C141","C153"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 Caco-2 data for sulfamethoxazole show moderate A-B permeability (4.5 ± 0.29 ×10^-6 cm/s) with no meaningful efflux (ER 1.3) and high mass balance (C224; duplicated as C188/C182).",
      "card_ids": ["C224"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 records show sulfamethoxazole undergoes CYP2C9-mediated N4-hydroxylation (C244, C275) with genotype-dependent in vitro Clint values (e.g., wild-type recombinant 27.8 ± 10.1 µl/nmol, C229; human liver microsomes 0.68 ± 0.37 µl/nmol/min, C248), but these are pathway-specific intrinsic-clearance measurements, not total hepatic extraction or in vivo F, and do not affirm F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C244","C275","C229","C248"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 high HLM Clint values for non-query isoxazole sulfonamides (17-203 µL/min/mg; C270, C238, C258, C236) are structurally distinct benzylic sulfonamides and are not transferable as low-F evidence for the anilino sulfonamide query.",
      "card_ids": ["C270","C238","C258","C236"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C229","C244","C248","C275","C270","C238","C258","C236"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for sulfisoxazole or sulfamethoxazole is supplied in the records.",
    "No total hepatic clearance, hepatic extraction ratio, or in vivo first-pass data are supplied for the query or closest analog; L6 CYP2C9 N-hydroxylation Clint values are pathway-specific.",
    "Transfer is analogical; no context exactly matches the 3,4-dimethyl-5-isoxazolyl sulfanilamide scaffold.",
    "Formulation effects are unknown; enteric-coated PAS had 0% relative bioavailability (C64, C70), so formulation could modify exposure.",
    "Species and condition differences add uncertainty in extrapolation."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high because L3-L5 evidence for the closest sulfanilamide-isoxazole analog (sulfamethoxazole) and related sulfonamides shows high oral absorption and substantial systemic exposure, with no meaningful efflux; L6 CYP2C9 metabolism records are pathway-specific and do not provide affirmative threshold-relevant evidence for F < 20%. The physicochemical prior (low neutral fraction, high TPSA) is not sufficient to overturn this."
}

